# Build context is this directory: compose declares `context: .` from here, and
# the Dockerfile's own header documents the same root for the standalone
# `crawlutron` repo ("the repository root where this Dockerfile lives"). Every
# pattern below is therefore context-relative, so this file is correct whether
# the service sits in a monorepo subdirectory or is the repo root.
#
# An allowlist, not a denylist, for two reasons. The image is built from exactly
# five sources (listed at the bottom), and an allowlist states that as a fact
# rather than guessing what some future directory might weigh. And it cannot go
# stale: the local-only trees this context used to ship -- .venv alone was 771 MB
# of an 867 MB context, alongside cache/, logs/, tmp/, report/, .cortexkit/,
# .mypy_cache/, .pytest_cache/ -- are all excluded by the leading `*` without
# being named, so none of them needs a line here to stay out. Being wrong costs
# a loud `COPY failed: not found`, never a silently missing file.
#
# The five sources, from the Dockerfile's own COPY lines:
#   pyproject.toml            builder, camoufox-binary, development
#   uv.lock                   builder, camoufox-binary, development
#   crawlutron/               runtime
#   uvicorn-log-config.json   runtime
#   Dockerfile                the build itself
*
!crawlutron/
!crawlutron/**
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!uvicorn-log-config.json
!Dockerfile

# `!crawlutron/**` re-admits local bytecode sitting beside the source, which the leading
# `*` had already excluded, so it has to be excluded again after the negation.
# These are stale .pyc files for sources edited since they were written.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]